 "verdict": "KILL the +24.21 bp at 1D as a quoted claim, on REPRODUCIBILITY and UNIT grounds, not on the cost test. It is (a) unit-ambiguous between per-trade and per-year - a factor of 365 - and gross/net ambiguous, and (b) unreproducible: no horizon-ladder implementation exists in either repo, so four documents cite a number nobody can recompute. G-COST-3 cannot settle it because a 21.07bp mid-venue round trip lands INSIDE the kill range while 2.00, 11.08, 26.00 and 56.04bp land outside - the rule is firing on cost regime, not on the claim. What survives is the ladder arithmetic: annual cost drag = 365/holding_days x round_trip_bps, so a 15m hold at a 21bp round turn pays ~2,450pct of notional a year in friction against ~17pct for a 1D hold. THAT is the defensible horizon claim, and it needs no unstated figure to make it."
